Hermit kernel (hermit-rs tag hermit-0.13.0, kernel ef27b79): run on the virtual
timer on aarch64, for Chitala's Native partitioning spike (N1.4).

Upstream, the kernel programs the EL1 physical timer (CNTP_*) and reads the
physical counter. Under a hypervisor that runs several guests on one CPU, as
seL4 does in N1.4, the physical timer is one register set that every guest
would program over the others'; the virtual timer (CNTV_*) is what the
hypervisor saves and restores for each vCPU, and whose interrupt it injects.
With this patch the kernel uses the virtual timer and counter, and takes the
device tree's virtual timer interrupt. Without a hypervisor the virtual
offset is zero: the virtual timer is the physical one. native/run.sh applies
it after the RNDR patch; it is carried (spike-only).

